			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Expand extension root discovery and modularize telemetry/hover units\n\nExtend the LocalhostPlugin to resolve built-in extensions from multiple distribution paths (`Contents/Resources/extensions`, `Contents/Resources/app/extensions`) and the development monorepo layout. This ensures icon stylesheets for the 93 bundled extensions render correctly in packaged `.app` builds and prevents empty boxes in the extension view.\n\nApply the established distributed architecture pattern to the PostHog analytics and Hover command subsystems. Refactor `PostHogPlugin` and `Command/Hover` into distinct unit files (e.g., `Initialize::Fn`, `Position::Struct`, `HoverContent::Enum`), enforcing PascalCase naming and separating DTO definitions from logic. This aligns with recent telemetry refactors and prepares the codebase for stricter IPC type safety.\n\nImpact: Fixes extension icon rendering in production builds and standardizes the module structure for observability and LSP features.",
			"SHA": "0bb57d42016d8ab3ea6bc79312fdbcb8681e2657"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:30:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1251,
				13
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize telemetry gate subsystem into distinct units\n\nRestructure the `Source/Telemetry/Gates` module to align with CodeEditorLand's PascalCase naming conventions and the established distributed architecture pattern.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Extract compile-time predicates (`IsDebugBuild`, `IsDevelopmentBuild`, `IsTelemetryEnabled`, `IsMetricsEnabled`, `IsDistributedTracingEnabled`, `IsFeatureFlagsEnabled`) into dedicated `Fn` unit files using `cfg!` macros.\n- Isolate runtime gate management (`RuntimeGates`, `GetRuntimeGates`, `RuntimeGateEnabled`, `ListEnabledGates`, `ValidateRequiredGates`) into separate units sharing a private `GATES` singleton.\n- Convert `EnableRuntimeGate` into a no-op `Fn` shim with documentation noting the required migration from `OnceLock<HashSet>` to `RwLock` for mutable state.\n- Update `mod.rs` to export the new flat structure, removing the previous monolithic implementation.\n\nThis reorganization ensures strict adherence to project naming standards and prepares the gate system for runtime configuration injection and IPC integration.\n\nRefs #Telemetry",
			"SHA": "2a691e34b07b06fa7cc73d6c99d68b16635230a0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:30:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1239,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize tracing subsystem into distinct utility units\n\nRestructure the `Source/Telemetry/Tracing` module to align with CodeEditorLand's PascalCase naming conventions and modular design principles. Replace the previous monolithic implementation with a distributed architecture where each concept resides in its own file.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Extract `CreateSpan::Fn`, `InitializeTracing::Fn`, `InstrumentRPC::Fn`, `InstrumentCommand::Fn`, and `MeasureTime` macro into dedicated unit files.\n- Enforce feature-gated compilation so the `Telemetry` flag completely toggles the system on/off with zero overhead in release builds.\n- Standardize function names to `Fn` and maintain strict separation between span creation, RPC wrapping, command instrumentation, and inline timing macros.\n- Update `mod.rs` to export the new structure and simplify the public API surface.\n\nThis reorganization ensures strict adherence to project naming standards and prepares the observability layer for future integration into the IPC hot paths and binary entry point.\n\nRefs #Telemetry",
			"SHA": "ceb085c32354e6cfeb53302f933fe3d527606057"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T09:26:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1234,
				10
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Refactor metrics subsystem into modular singleton architecture\n\nRestructure the `Source/Telemetry/Metrics` module to align with CodeEditorLand's PascalCase naming conventions and modular design principles. Replace the previous single-file implementation with a distributed architecture where each concept resides in its own file.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Extract `Metric::Struct` and `MetricValue::Enum` into dedicated type definitions.\n- Isolate the `MetricsRegistry::Struct` (bounded ring buffer) and `GlobalRegistry::REGISTRY` singleton into separate units.\n- Introduce `Timer::Struct` for RAII-style histogram recording with label support.\n- Create convenience accessors `RecordCounter::Fn`, `RecordGauge::Fn`, and `GetAllMetrics::Fn` that operate against the global singleton.\n- Update `mod.rs` to export the new structure and add `Initialize::Fn` for feature-gated bootstrapping.\n\nThis reorganization ensures strict adherence to the project's naming standards (e.g., `Fn`, `Struct`, `REGISTRY`) and prepares the telemetry layer for future integration with the IPC fast paths and binary main entry point.",
			"SHA": "adbf0e3f64efb9475766d21b6c343e9f24a608d2"
		},
